.TH "REPROCTL\-AUTONOMY" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-autonomy \- durable local claim, status, and control state
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]reproctl autonomy\f[R] \f[I]subcommand\f[R] [\f[I]options\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage durable local state for autonomous orchestration.
.PP
The autonomy surface records local claims, active runs, retry metadata,
and Linear sync state for operator workflows.
It does not provide a web UI.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
\f[B]status\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-all\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]]
Show current claims and runs.
With \f[B]\-\-json\f[R], emits a machine\-readable status object.
.TP
\f[B]release\f[R] \f[I]issue\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-reason\f[R] \f[I]text\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]]
Release a local claim so it can be picked up again.
.TP
\f[B]cancel\f[R] \f[I]issue\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-reason\f[R] \f[I]text\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]]
Mark a claim canceled locally and sync the issue out of active work.
.TP
\f[B]retry\f[R] \f[I]issue\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-phase\f[R] \f[I]observe\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-claimed\-by\f[R] \f[I]name\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-reason\f[R] \f[I]text\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]]
Reset retryable local state and re\-prepare the issue.
.TP
\f[B]reconcile\f[R] [\f[I]issue\f[R] | \f[B]\-\-all\f[R]]
Refresh local claims from Linear issue state.
.TP
\f[B]discover\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-limit\f[R] \f[I]count\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-profile\f[R] \f[I]name\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-prompt\-file\f[R] \f[I]path\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-output\-dir\f[R] \f[I]path\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-claimed\-by\f[R] \f[I]name\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-project\f[R] \f[I]name\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]]
Build a discovery wave, run OpenCode, and write durable discovery
artifacts.
.TP
\f[B]run start\f[R] \f[I]issue\f[R] \f[B]\-\-phase\f[R] \f[I]phase\f[R] \f[B]\-\-workspace\f[R] \f[I]path\f[R]
Start a durable run attempt.
.TP
\f[B]run finish\f[R] \f[I]issue\f[R] \f[B]\-\-attempt\f[R] \f[I]n\f[R] \f[B]\-\-state\f[R] \f[I]state\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-error\f[R] \f[I]text\f[R]]
Finish a run attempt and capture any failure message.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-all\f[R]
Include released and canceled claims in status output.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-reason\f[R] \f[I]text\f[R]
Explain why a claim was released, canceled, or retried.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-phase\f[R] \f[I]phase\f[R]
Set the preparation phase for retry and run commands.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-claimed\-by\f[R] \f[I]name\f[R]
Tag local claim ownership with an operator name.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-profile\f[R] \f[I]name\f[R]
Pass a specific OpenCode profile to the launcher.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-prompt\-file\f[R] \f[I]path\f[R]
Use an alternate discovery prompt template.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-output\-dir\f[R] \f[I]path\f[R]
Override the discovery artifact directory.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-project\f[R] \f[I]name\f[R]
Restrict discovery to a Linear project.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]
Emit machine\-readable JSON instead of a short text summary.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
reproctl autonomy status \-\-json
Inspect claims, runs, retry state, and recent sync errors.
.TP
reproctl autonomy retry REP\-123 \-\-phase observe \-\-claimed\-by autopilot
Rebuild a stale claim and resume work.
